# What Vercel needs to run the API and the web UI: api/, sentinel/, frontend/, samples/, requirements.txt. Nothing else.
#
# pyproject.toml is hidden from Vercel ON PURPOSE. When a project has both pyproject.toml and requirements.txt (and no
# lockfile), Vercel's Python builder installs from pyproject.toml. Ours lists no dependencies, because the scanner is
# standard-library only, so FastAPI was never installed and every request failed with 500 FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED.
# Hidden, the builder falls back to requirements.txt (pinned) and finds the app in api/index.py.
pyproject.toml
requirements-dev.txt

archive/
tests/
bench/
docs/
demo/
action/
spec/
vscode-extension/
.github/
.sentinel/
AGENTS.lock
AGENTS.lock.sig
Makefile
setup.sh
*.md
!frontend/README.md
!samples/**
